    "FuncDef": "The ipv4-family vpnv4 command enables the BGP-VPNv4 address family and displays the address family view.\nThe undo ipv4-family vpnv4 command deletes the configurations in the BGP-VPNv4 address family.\nBy default, the BGP-IPv4 unicast address family view is displayed.",
    "CLIs": [
        "ipv4-family vpnv4",
        "undo ipv4-family vpnv4"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "BGP multi-instance view"
    ],
    "ParaDef": null,
    "Examples": [
        [
            "<HUAWEI> system-view",
            "[~HUAWEI] bgp 100 instance a",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp-instance-a] ipv4-family vpnv4"
        ]
    ],
    "ExtraInfo": "Usage Scenario\nThe ipv4-family vpnv4 command enables the BGP-VPNv4 address family and displays the address family view.\nConfiguration Impact\nTo disable the IPv4 unicast address family, run the undo default ipv4-unicast command.\nPrecautions\nThe undo ipv4-family command cannot delete the BGP-IPv4 unicast address family view.\nIf the undo ipv4-family command is run, the VPN target and IPv4 configurations of the VPN are deleted. Therefore, exercise caution when running this command."
}
