{
    "PageTitle": "default local-preference (BGP IPv6 SR-Policy address family view)",
    "FuncDef": "The default local-preference command configures a Local_Pref for BGP routes.\nThe undo default local-preference command restores the default value.\nBy default, the Local_Pref of BGP routes is 100.",
    "CLIs": [
        "default local-preference <preference>",
        "undo default local-preference"
    ],
    "ParentView": [
        "BGP IPv6 SR-Policy address family view"
    ],
    "ParaDef": [
        {
            "Parameters": "preference",
            "Info": "Specifies a Local_Pref for BGP routes. The larger the value, the higher the priority.\nThe value is an integer ranging from 0 to 4294967295."
        }
    ],
    "Examples": [
        [
            "<HUAWEI> system-view",
            "[~HUAWEI] bgp 100",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp] ipv6-family sr-policy",
            "[*HUAWEI-bgp-af-ipv6-srpolicy] default local-preference 200"
        ]
    ],
    "ExtraInfo": "Usage Scenario\nLocal_Pref is used to determine the optimal route for the traffic that leaves an AS. If BGP receives from different IBGP peers multiple routes to the same destination address but with different next hops, it selects the route with the largest Local_Pref value.\nConfiguration Impact\nIf more than one Local_Pref is configured for BGP routes, the latest configuration overrides the previous one.\nPrecautions\nThe Local_Pref is valid among IBGP peers and is not advertised to other ASs."
}
